Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Ensure subprocess UTF-8 decoding and MSVC include readiness on Windows

Reason: On Windows systems with non-UTF8 ANSI code pages (such as GBK/cp936),
invoking `subprocess.run(..., capture_output=True, text=True)` without explicit
`encoding="utf-8"` or `errors="replace"` causes `_readerthread` in Python's
subprocess module to crash with `UnicodeDecodeError` when ffprobe or ffmpeg
emits UTF-8 metadata. Additionally, having `cl.exe` in PATH without `INCLUDE`
containing `<array>` causes `_activate_msvc` to skip `vcvars64.bat` activation,
leading to compilation errors in AOT Inductor.

Removal: Delete once upstream applies explicit UTF-8 subprocess decoding on media
helpers and checks MSVC include readiness before skipping vcvars.

diff --git a/src/finesub/media/ffmpeg.py b/src/finesub/media/ffmpeg.py
index 2cfdee3..dfdce91 100644
--- a/src/finesub/media/ffmpeg.py
+++ b/src/finesub/media/ffmpeg.py
@@ -85,7 +85,13 @@ def _format_seconds(seconds: float) -> str:
 
 
 def _run_ffmpeg(args: list[str]) -> None:
-    result = subprocess.run(args, capture_output=True, text=True)
+    result = subprocess.run(
+        args,
+        capture_output=True,
+        text=True,
+        encoding="utf-8",
+        errors="replace",
+    )
     if result.returncode != 0:
         detail = (result.stderr or result.stdout or "").strip()
         raise RuntimeError(f"ffmpeg failed (exit {result.returncode}): {detail}")
@@ -111,6 +117,8 @@ def probe_media_duration(
         ],
         capture_output=True,
         text=True,
+        encoding="utf-8",
+        errors="replace",
     )
     if result.returncode != 0:
         detail = (result.stderr or result.stdout or "").strip()
@@ -144,6 +152,8 @@ def media_has_video_stream(
         ],
         capture_output=True,
         text=True,
+        encoding="utf-8",
+        errors="replace",
     )
     if result.returncode != 0:
         detail = (result.stderr or result.stdout or "").strip()
